      "statement": "Wake-on-LAN builds a magic packet of six 0xFF bytes followed by the MAC repeated sixteen times and sends it by UDP broadcast to ports 7 and 9, to both the global broadcast address and the broadcast address of the TV's /24 subnet, succeeding if at least one send worked and raising a connection error if none did.",
